# The web member app was restored in 2026-08 (docs/PRODUCT.md#web-app-status)
# and lives at /app, not at /: the root stays the marketing page, which is what
# the Google Ads campaign points at. Member slugs (/patrick) are deliberately
# NOT listed here: they fall through the catch-all as a 200 rewrite so the URL
# survives, which is what lets iOS/macOS resolve them against
# .well-known/apple-app-site-association and open the app instead of ever
# fetching the page. A 301 here would still work on Apple devices but would
# throw away the member context on every other one.
#
# Retired for real — member approval went away in 2026-08 (migration 058) and
# these have no page behind them any more.
/join     /         301
/setup    /members  301
/requests /members  301
/admin    /members  301

# Everything else (member slugs, stale bookmarks, old SPA deep links) renders
# the app without changing the URL. Real files win over this rule, so /,
# /privacy, /terms, /groups and friends still serve themselves.
/*  /app.html  200
